    "variable": "line + (cptr - buf) + strlen(cptr) + 1",
    "missing_conjunct": "line + (cptr - buf) + strlen(cptr) + 1 <= line + strlen(line)",
    "criterion": "Before `snmp_config_when()` calls `skip_white()`, the computed `start_from` pointer must not advance past the terminating NUL of the original `line` string.",
    "description": "The vulnerable execution reparses the remembered `\" 1\"` line and reuses the token offset from the stack copy against the original heap string without clamping the result. That leaves `line + (cptr - buf) + strlen(cptr) + 1` one byte past `line + strlen(line)`, while the fixed execution clamps the same expression back to the string end before `skip_white()` runs."
  },
